  "prediction": "President Donald Trump held a 80-minute press conference on Thursday, addressing various topics and controversies surrounding his administration. The event was marked by Trump's combative and defensive tone, as he sparred with reporters and dismissed facts.\n\nTrump began by blaming former President Barack Obama for the state of the country, saying he \"inherited a mess.\" He also claimed that Republicans are close to repealing and replacing Obamacare, with a plan to be submitted by mid-March.\n\nOn the topic of Russia, Trump denied directing former national security adviser Michael Flynn to discuss sanctions with Russian officials. He also stated that there is no comparison between WikiLeaks and U.S. government leaks, and that Hillary Clinton's \"stupid\" uranium deal with Russia was a major mistake.\n\nTrump's comments on the media were a major focus of the press conference. He repeatedly accused the press of being \"dishonest\" and \"fake news,\" and claimed that the public no longer trusts the media. He also stated that he would be a good reporter, saying \"I'd be a pretty good reporter, not as good as you.\"\n\nTrump's performance was widely criticized by historians and experts, who noted that he had never before publicly maligned the press or attacked reporters by name. The event was seen as a continuation of Trump's campaign theme of attacking the media, and was cheered by his supporters.\n\nIn other news, Trump's administration has been plagued by controversy and dysfunction, with the forced resignation of Flynn and a defeat in court. Trump's approval ratings are lower than those of past presidents at the same point in their administrations, with 39% of Americans approving of his job performance and 56% disapproving.\n\nTrump's comments on immigration were also notable, as he blamed Homeland Security Secretary James Kelly for the travel ban executive order rollout and stated that he would \"deal with DACA with heart.\" He also claimed that his White House is a \"fine-tuned machine,\" despite reports of chaos and dysfunction.\n\nThe press conference was seen as an attempt by Trump to regain control of the narrative and defend his administration's early days. However, it was widely criticized for its lack of substance and Trump's continued attacks on the media.\n\nKey moments from the press conference included:\n\n* Trump's denial of directing Flynn to discuss sanctions with Russian officials\n* Trump's claim that there is no comparison between WikiLeaks and U.S. government leaks\n* Trump's repeated attacks on the media, calling them \"dishonest\" and \"fake news\"\n* Trump's statement that he would be a good reporter\n*",
